# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.

# Postgres. Local development runs against Docker; production is a managed
# instance co-located with the app.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://taptap3d:taptap3d@localhost:5432/taptap3d

# ── SIGN-IN, WHICH IS HOW SOMEBODY GETS IN ─────────────────────────────────
#
# Google is the only provider and there is no password column anywhere in this
# product. Set BOTH of these and sign-in becomes the front door: the shared
# gate below is ignored, every page requires a session, and every decision is
# recorded against a named person rather than against the gate identity.
#
# LEAVE THEM EMPTY and the application behaves exactly as it did before
# sign-in existed. That is a supported state, not a degraded one — every
# end-to-end spec in this repository builds a sale against a local server, and
# a developer cloning this cannot be asked for a Google project first.
#
# To create them: Google Cloud console → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth
# client ID → Web application. The authorised redirect URI must be EXACTLY the
# origin plus /api/auth/google/callback, with no trailing slash — a mismatch
# is the commonest way this fails and Google's error names neither value.
#
#   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/google/callback      (local)
#   https://taptap3d.fly.dev/api/auth/google/callback   (deployed)
#
# Nobody is admitted by having a Google account: a `memberships` row must
# already exist for their address (src/lib/auth/admit.ts).
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The origin to build that redirect URI from, when the application cannot
# trust the request's own headers. Fly terminates TLS and forwards http, so
# without this the callback URI would say `http://` and Google would refuse
# it. Set it on any deployment behind a proxy; leave it empty locally.
#
#   TAPTAP3D_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://taptap3d.fly.dev
TAPTAP3D_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=

# Which house this deployment acts for, when more than one exists. Fly stays
# pinned to a single org while the move to GCP is planned, so this is set
# there; a person's own memberships decide it everywhere else.
TAPTAP3D_ORG_SLUG=

# THE M0 ACCESS GATE — not authentication, and not a substitute for it.
#
# A single shared secret in front of the whole deployed application, so a public
# URL is not a public database while the real identity system is deferred
# (ROADMAP D14). The predecessor shipped to the public internet with no gate at
# all and an unauthenticated DELETE endpoint; that is what this prevents.
#
# SUPERSEDED BY SIGN-IN WHEN ONE IS CONFIGURED. With GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET set, src/proxy.ts does not look at these at all — a
# browser credential box in front of a sign-in page is two doors for one room,
# and the first thing a prospect would see. They remain the answer for a
# staging box that has no Google project.
#
# Leave GATE_PASSWORD empty in local development to disable the gate.
GATE_USER=taptap3d
GATE_PASSWORD=

# THE PRINT PDF NEEDS A BROWSER, and this is how a developer machine finds one.
# The container image installs Chromium and sets this itself; leave it empty
# locally and the export answers 503 with that explanation rather than failing
# somewhere inside a library. Playwright's browser works if you have it:
#   node -e "console.log(require('playwright').chromium.executablePath())"
PUPPETEER_EXECUTABLE_PATH=
